# ========================================
# OUI SECURITY GUIDE - SECRET MANAGEMENT
# ========================================
# This file provides guidance on secure secret management for OUI

# ========================================
# 🚨 CRITICAL SECURITY REMINDERS
# ========================================
# 1. Never commit .env files to version control
# 2. Use different secrets for each environment (dev/staging/prod)
# 3. Rotate secrets regularly, especially after team changes
# 4. Use secret management systems in production

# ========================================
# SECRET MANAGEMENT OPTIONS
# ========================================

## 1. GitHub Secrets (for CI/CD)
# Set these in your GitHub repository settings:
# - DEPLOYMENT_PRIVATE_KEY
# - ETHERSCAN_API_KEY
# - INFURA_PROJECT_ID
# - MONGODB_URI
# - REDIS_URL
# - JWT_SECRET
# - ENCRYPTION_KEY

## 2. AWS Secrets Manager (Production)
# Store structured secrets:
# - oui-blockchain-secrets (RPC URLs, private keys)
# - oui-api-secrets (API keys, JWT secrets)
# - oui-database-secrets (DB credentials)

## 3. HashiCorp Vault (Enterprise)
# Use dynamic secret generation and rotation:
# - Blockchain secrets engine for private keys
# - Database secrets engine for DB credentials
# - KV secrets engine for API keys

## 4. Docker Secrets (Containerized)
# For local development with docker-compose:
# docker-compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.secrets.yml up

## 5. Kubernetes Secrets (Production)
# Already configured in k8s/production/:
# - oui-secrets (main application secrets)
# - mongodb-secret (database credentials)
# - redis-secret (Redis configuration)

# ========================================
# SECRET GENERATION COMMANDS
# ========================================

## Generate JWT Secret (32 bytes, hex encoded)
openssl rand -hex 32

## Generate Encryption Key (32 bytes, base64 encoded)
openssl rand -base64 32

## Generate Private Key (Ethereum wallet)
# Use a new wallet for each environment:
npx hardhat node --help  # Shows account generation

## Generate Database Password
openssl rand -base64 16

# ========================================
# ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATION
# ========================================

## Development Environment
# - Use local secrets files (not committed)
# - Simple passwords acceptable for local dev
# - Use local blockchain node (Hardhat/Ganache)

## Staging Environment
# - Use GitHub Secrets for CI/CD
# - Test with production-like secret management
# - Use testnet blockchain networks

## Production Environment
# - Use AWS Secrets Manager or HashiCorp Vault
# - Enable secret rotation
# - Use mainnet blockchain networks
# - Enable audit logging for secret access

# ========================================
# SECURITY CHECKLIST
# ========================================
# [ ] Different secrets for each environment
# [ ] Private keys are unique per environment
# [ ] API keys are stored securely
# [ ] Database passwords are strong (12+ chars)
# [ ] JWT secrets are cryptographically strong
# [ ] Secret rotation is configured
# [ ] Access logging is enabled
# [ ] .env files are not in version control
# [ ] Team members know how to access secrets
# [ ] Backup secrets are securely stored

# ========================================
# EMERGENCY PROCEDURES
# ========================================

## If Secrets Are Compromised:
# 1. Immediately rotate all affected secrets
# 2. Check for unauthorized transactions on blockchain
# 3. Review access logs for unauthorized access
# 4. Notify team members of the breach
# 5. Update incident response documentation

## Regular Security Maintenance:
# - Rotate JWT secrets monthly
# - Rotate private keys quarterly
# - Review secret access logs weekly
# - Update API keys when team members change

